Relevant columns & how they will be used  

• "project_short_name": filter rows to breast‑cancer project ‘TCGA‑BRCA’.  
• "chromosome": needed to bin segments by chromosomal location (later by cytoband once that table is located).  
• "start_pos", "end_pos": segment genomic coordinates – will be overlapped with cytoband coordinates; their difference gives segment length.  
• "segment_mean": log2( CN / 2 ); will be converted to absolute copy number, rounded, and finally classified (0,1,2,3,>3).  
• "case_barcode": patient identifier – used to count how many cases carry a given CNV type in a given cytoband.  
• "sample_barcode", "aliquot_barcode": let us separate multiple samples / aliquots per case when necessary.  
• "case_gdc_id", "sample_gdc_id", "aliquot_gdc_id": stable UUID versions of the barcodes – useful for joining to other GDC tables.  
• "num_probes": sometimes used to down‑weight very small‑probe segments.  
• "file_gdc_id": enables restriction to Release‑23 files if the file table is joined later.

Typical filter conditions  

1. "project_short_name" = 'TCGA‑BRCA'              – keep only breast cancer rows.  
2. "segment_mean" IS NOT NULL                      – avoid missing CN estimates.  
3. "segment_mean" > 1.5 OR < –1.5                  – fetch clear amplifications / deletions.  
4. "chromosome" IN ('chr1','chr2', … ,'chrX')      – keep autosomes + chrX.  
5. "case_barcode" ILIKE 'TCGA‑BRCA%'               – rarely useful because the study abbreviation already appears in project.  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20) that progressively build familiarity with the copy‑number table; every identifier is in double quotes.

```sql
-- 1. Description: List every distinct TCGA project present in the CN segment table.
SELECT DISTINCT "project_short_name"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show the first 20 BRCA rows to understand the column contents.
SELECT *
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Retrieve the distinct chromosomes represented in TCGA‑BRCA data.
SELECT DISTINCT "chromosome"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
ORDER BY "chromosome"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: List 20 distinct case barcodes for BRCA.
SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Count how many copy‑number segments each case has (first 20 cases shown).
SELECT "case_barcode",
       COUNT(*) AS "segment_count"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
GROUP BY "case_barcode"
ORDER BY "segment_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Average segment_mean per chromosome across all BRCA segments (20 chromosomes displayed).
SELECT "chromosome",
       AVG("segment_mean") AS "avg_log2_cn"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
GROUP BY "chromosome"
ORDER BY "chromosome"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: For one sample, show segment length and absolute copy number estimate.
SELECT "sample_barcode",
       "chromosome",
       "start_pos",
       "end_pos",
       ("end_pos" - "start_pos" + 1) AS "segment_length_bp",
       ROUND(POWER(2, "segment_mean") * 2, 2) AS "estimated_copy_number"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_barcode" = (
        SELECT DISTINCT "sample_barcode"
        FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
        WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
        LIMIT 1
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Identify high‑level amplifications (rounded CN > 3) in BRCA.
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "chromosome",
       "start_pos",
       "end_pos",
       ROUND(POWER(2, "segment_mean") * 2) AS "rounded_cn"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND ROUND(POWER(2, "segment_mean") * 2) > 3
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Show frequency of segments whose rounded CN equals 0 (homozygous deletion) among BRCA segments.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "homdel_segment_count",
       ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(*) / (
           SELECT COUNT(*)
           FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
           WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
       ), 2) AS "homdel_percentage"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND ROUND(POWER(2, "segment_mean") * 2) = 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Compute an overlap‑weighted average copy number per chromosome per case (simplified, 20 rows).
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "chromosome",
       ROUND(
           SUM( ("end_pos" - "start_pos" + 1) * (POWER(2, "segment_mean") * 2) ) /
           SUM( ("end_pos" - "start_pos" + 1) )
       , 2) AS "wtd_avg_cn"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
GROUP BY "case_barcode", "chromosome"
LIMIT 20;
```

These queries expose the key data elements needed to build the final cytoband‑level CNV frequency analysis.
